1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
PACKLIGHT  |  A reusable packing checklist
Track 01: Does naming the checklist help visitors take the first step?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:17,000
A: “Get started”  →  B: “Open my packing checklist”
Hypothesis: naming the checklist lifts first-visit opens by at least 15%.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The CTA opens a working checklist with locally saved progress.
Flagsmith records checklist_opened against the same anonymous identity.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,000
One enabled multivariate Flagsmith flag: packlight_checklist_cta
100% enrollment, 50/50 allocation, one occurrence metric.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:48,000
1,800 synthetic visits through the real app routes.
The simulator assumed 24% control clicks and 37% treatment clicks.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Specific: 348/923 (37.70%)  |  Control: 213/877 (24.29%)
Native Flagsmith result: +55.24% relative lift, >99% chance to win.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Completed in Flagsmith: rolled out “specific” on the same flag.
SDK verification: 20 fresh and 2 returning identities got the winner.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
A fresh visit now gets “Open my packing checklist.” No redeploy.
Synthetic result only. Find the evidence and tests in the public repo.
